% session1_thick_as_thieves: a Picat model from DCP Rosetta.
%
% Following a robbery at Sparkles the Jeweller's, Inspector Korner of the Yard interviewed six of the usual suspects.
% He knew that the getaway car had been barely big enough to hold two, so he reckoned that at least four of them were
% innocent - but which ones? He also supposed that the innocent ones would tell the truth, while the guilty one or
% ones would lie. What they actually said was:
% - ARTIE: "It wasn't me."
% - BILL: "Crackitt was in it up to his neck."
% - CRACKITT: "No I wasn't."
% - DODGY: "If Crackitt did it, Bill did it with him."
% - EDGY: "Nobody did it alone."
% - FINGERS: "That's right: it was Artie and Dodgy together."
% If the good inspector's suppositions were correct, who is guilty?
%
%   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session1_thick_as_thieves.html
% Save this model as model.pi and run it (Picat 3.9, https://picat-lang.org) with:
%   picat model.pi

% The puzzle has no data: each suspect is a decision variable, 1 when guilty.
import cp.

model(_Data, Vars, Outputs, Options) =>
    Suspects = [Artie, Bill, Crackitt, Dodgy, Edgy, Fingers],
    Suspects :: 0..1,
    % at least four of the six are innocent, so at most two are guilty
    sum(Suspects) #=< 2,
    % a suspect is guilty exactly when what he said is false, since the innocent tell the truth and the guilty lie
    % Artie: "It wasn't me." is false exactly when Artie is guilty
    Artie #<=> #~ (#~ Artie),
    % Bill: "Crackitt was in it up to his neck." is false exactly when Crackitt is innocent
    Bill #<=> #~ Crackitt,
    % Crackitt: "No I wasn't." is false exactly when Crackitt is guilty
    Crackitt #<=> #~ (#~ Crackitt),
    % Dodgy: "If Crackitt did it, Bill did it with him." is false exactly when Crackitt is guilty and Bill is innocent
    Dodgy #<=> #~ (Crackitt #=> Bill),
    % Edgy: "Nobody did it alone." is false exactly when exactly one suspect is guilty
    Edgy #<=> #~ (sum(Suspects) #!= 1),
    % Fingers: "That's right: it was Artie and Dodgy together." is false exactly when not both Artie and Dodgy are guilty
    Fingers #<=> #~ (Artie #/\ Dodgy),
    Vars = Suspects,
    Outputs = [artie = Artie, bill = Bill, crackitt = Crackitt, dodgy = Dodgy,
               edgy = Edgy, fingers = Fingers],
    Options = [].

main =>
    model(new_map(), Vars, Outputs, Options),
    solve(Options, Vars),
    solve(vars(Outputs)),
    foreach(Name = Value in Outputs)
        printf("%w = %w\n", Name, Value)
    end.
